      "text": "To find: $x^2 + y^2 + z^2.$\n\nSince $\\mathbb{M} = (2, 3, 4), \\mathbb{M}^*(2, 3, 4)$.\n\nThus, $\\mathbb{M} \\cdot \\mathbb{M}^*$ = Function.\n$\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 2y & z \\\\ x & y & -z \\\\ x & -y & z \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & x & x \\\\ 2y & y & -y \\\\ z & -z & z \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} x & x & x \\\\ x & x & x \\\\ x & x & x \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\Rightarrow x=y=z= \\pm 1.$\n\nHence, $x^2+y^2+z^2=\\boxed{1}.$\nThe answer is: 1",
