      "text": "$(\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M})_{11} = 0^2 + x^2 + z^2$\n$(\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M})_{12} = x + 2yz,$\n$(\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M})_{13} = zx - yz,$\n$(\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M})_{21} = x^2 + y^2 + z^2,$\n$(\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M})_{22} = x^2 + y^2 + z^2$\n$(\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M})_{23} = zx - yz,$\n$(\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M})_{31} = x + y - z,$\n$(\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M})_{32} = x^2 + y^2 + z^2,$\n$(\\mathbf{M}^T \\mathbf{M})_{33} = x^2 + y^2 + z^2.$\nThis implies\n\\begin{align*}\n2(x^2 + y^2 + z^2) &= (x + 2yz)^2. \\quad \\boxed{x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = \\frac{2}{5}}.\n\\end{align*}. The answer is \\frac{2}{5}",
